Z||000002||batboy||01-21-2000||09:44 PM||||I have a 15 pound, blue-eyed, slightly cross-eyed cat named Grizzly, that can kick butt on all of the neighborhood cats and most of the dogs.<P> <IMG SRC="http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/YAWNING2.jpg"> <P>Actually, he's just yawning in the pic. He is the best pet I've ever had and we are best buddies. In the house he's Mr. Mellow, purrs a lot, and is very well behaved.<P>He showed up at my home in 1997 as a flea bitten, worm infested, chewed up, hungry, and very pathetic looking stray tomcat. I took pity on him, gave him food and water, and took him to visit the vet. After we bonded and he decided to adopted me, Grizzly kept me from being lonely and caught all the vicious, evil mice that were lurking around the place.||||reg||1
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||01-21-2000||09:53 PM||||I have a 4 year old Boxer. He weighs in at 85 lbs. and is wearing fawn fur with white sox and has a white chest. His ears are done and when he stands in front of the TV in our bedroom (mine and my wife's bedroom)at night, all we can see is his outline. Looks like Batman...lol. He is a cool dog and I want to find him a girlfriend soon.||||reg||6
