Z||000020||william_thorniii||01-24-2000||12:55 PM||||I have only one pet of my own... a 75# Walker Coon Hound.  The breed is one of the better performing hounds due to their approximately 5 mile range of scent detection.  They are also known to continue hunting for an entire day without stopping.  His name is Duke after the Iron Duke... although he was in bad shape he just kept on running.  My fiancee and I found him while we were in high school.  At that time he was just under 40# and all muscle and bones.  He had gotten sprayed by a skunk while hunting and therefore couldn't find his way back.  So now, I have completely ruined the dog by making him a house and companion dog.  Needless to say, you can't see his ribs anymore.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000021||Cooter||01-24-2000||03:18 PM||||William,<BR>Thats pretty funny about getting the hound. Kind of the same way I got my beagle. She just showed up one day and wondered around the neighborhood. Finally my wife took her in because the beagle had almost got run over several times. Later I found out that she is a real bread of beagle called a DelRay Stubby and the original breader of the dogs has sold them for LOTS of money. They are supposed to be good rabbit dogs because they can get under shrubs and brush easily. The only thing she hunts is a warm spot for a nap!||||reg||1
Z||000022||william_thorniii||01-24-2000||03:23 PM||||Cooter,<P>Yup, that sounds like my Duke alright.  Odddly enough many vets and breeders have told me that he is of a good bloodline as well.  There is something about the coloring and the shape of the snout.  I don't care about that.  All that I know is that he is smartest dog that I have ever known.  He can open cabinets, drawers, swinging doors, etc.  And he has or will eat anything.  some examples are that he has eaten through steel cans trying to get food, he has eaten an entire 10# bag of potatoes, several quarter chickens and much too many others to list.  We have not found anything to this date that he will not eat if given the opportunity.<P>William T. Thorn, III   ||||reg||10
Z||000023||dogtired||01-24-2000||03:44 PM||||Can only share a sad story here?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>My best buddy Oliver passed away last January. He was a GREAT Great Dane, last time weighed he was 116lbs. Black with white spots? or was he white with black spots? He lived a real dogs life, I cut a hole in the garage door so he could come in and out whenever he wanted. Built a room 4 X 8 in corner of the garage with a full sizes matress in it. I also connected a vent from the HVAC system in the house so he had heat and A/C? He was a half inside half outside dog. He got a bath every other week, first week after the bath he stayed in the house the second week he stayed outside, if you can call his garage apartment outside? To give him a bath I would just walk over and tap on the side of the bath tub, he would look at me, lower his head and come over and step right in  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> What a DOG! he even helped me work on cars, many times when I would crawl under a vehicle he would get down on all 4's and be right there beside me. Often I would have to go out in the yard to pick up car parts, grease rags and tools. That reminds me of one particular greasey wheel bearing covered with slobber, I am here to tell you this guy could slime you in a heart beat  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Anyway he is gone now, old age, all I have left is photos and lots of fond memories  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Oliver was my BEST FRIEND! No other could take his place! May get another pup someday??<BR>And as I am sure Oliver thought "CATS! the other white Meat"   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000024||william_thorniii||01-24-2000||05:28 PM||||dog,<P>That is strange in a couple of ways.  I lost Samuel this year.  He was a 14 yr. old Dark Golden Retriever.  Although he was neither as smart nor as well mannered as your Oliver, he was a great dog.  I also find it odd since I have always wanted a Great Dane and one of the black and white ones... I believe that they are called harlequin.  Someday I hope to get one, but my fiancee is pushing for an Old English Bulldog.  ||||reg||9
